                    {
                        "sense_id": "64c2b4d9-ebb1-394d-872d-25e7ee20a077",
                        "entry_id": "60195b1c-c300-314f-96b2-adf9528875dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne intersexuée dotée précisément d’un ovaire et d’un testicule."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d8b4bee-0224-495e-9f62-f17c8ffaf711",
                                "sense_id": "64c2b4d9-ebb1-394d-872d-25e7ee20a077",
                                "text": "For some time medical investigators have recognized the concept of the intersexual body. But the standard medical literature uses the term intersex as a catch-all for three major subgroups with some mixture of male and female characteristics: the so-called true hermaphrodites, whom I call herms, who possess one testis and one ovary (the sperm- and egg-producing vessels, or gonads); […]"
